      "id": "",
      "text": "↳ one core-made clearing handle",
      "href": "#ownership",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "1\nMove the clearing mechanism into core.\nSTATED\n\nThe language-neutral scope is reusable. Each TypeScript service still constructs and owns its own scope; algorithms, source cache a",
      "href": "#ownership",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "2\nKeep six independent address spaces.\nSTATED\n\nOne scope, six typed handles, one map per handle. Existing keys and value types stay separate; a shared key never makes two query kin",
      "href": "#drawers",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "3\nKeep the exact entries and failure behavior.\nSTATED\n\nReuse values and promises, including empties; the new generic primitive also accepts undefined. Rejected promises stay cached",
      "href": "#entries",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "4\nFinish refresh before starting a turn.\nSTATED\n\nSuccessful refresh clears all six, even for unchanged files. A failed refresh never reaches that clearing step, preserving the curr",
      "href": "#lifecycle",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "5\nClear first; await project release next.\nSTATED\n\nClearing stays synchronous. The service now returns a promise and the backend awaits it, so a pending or rejected graph release r",
      "href": "#lifecycle",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "6\nClearing is reusable, not terminal.\nUNEXPLAINED\n\nNo turn token, cancellation, closed flag or query lock. Both signals empty the same registered handles; repeated clearing is allo",
      "href": "#reusable",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "7\nExpose a small cache API; pass fewer inputs.\nUNEXPLAINED\n\nCore exports the scope and lookup-only handle type. Handles expose no clearing operation. The service’s beginTurn takes ",
      "href": "#api",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "8\nCharacterize, then extract.\nSTATED\n\nFour new core tests and six new service tests pin the preservation contract. Five previous service tests remain with their assertions intact. ",
      "href": "#evidence",
      "visible": true
    },
